      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The reference class contains 12 distinct original-period official prints from July 2025 through June 2026. Its mean is 51.92%, with a range of 45% to 57%. This base rate establishes the historical level; June's 45% is the persistence anchor because the recent sequence indicates a lower current level."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Evidence limitation: the web tool could not fetch the raw CSV/API Georgia O rows and their exact ex parte numerators. HistoricalContext therefore contains the whole-percent values printed in archived CMS current-month snapshots, rather than reconstructed one-decimal ratios. These snapshots separate original monthly outcomes from quarterly updated outcomes; all historical anchors use the original-period variant. Final resolution still requires the exact first-published O numerator and denominator."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off, and policy effects are separated. June supplies the level. The five January-to-June changes average -1.8 percentage points per month. I apply half that momentum over the two-month horizon, a judgmental shrinkage toward persistence. One-off and new-policy adjustments are zero: Georgia's policy effective August 2025 already requires using electronic sources and related-case information for administrative MAGI renewals, and no fetched source establishes a new August 2026 automation shock. The July-to-August 2025 decline of 4 points is one seasonal observation, insufficient for a separate seasonal adjustment."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Model is June persistence plus 50%-damped recent momentum, using the 12 fetched original-period snapshot shares. Point = 45 + 0.5 * 2 * (-1.8) + 0 one-off + 0 policy = 43.2%. The 11 successive changes are [-4, 1, 0, 2, -4, 2, -1, -3, -2, -1, -2] percentage points; their mean is -1.09091 and squared deviations sum to 46.90909. Sample sigma = 2.16585 percentage points = sqrt(46.90909 / 10). The one-month normal 80% half-width is 1.28 * sigma = 2.77229 points. Allowing two unobserved monthly movements gives 2.77229 * sqrt(2) = 3.92061; adding 0.5 point for whole-percent anchor precision gives 4.42061. Bounds = 43.2 +/- 4.42061 = [38.77939, 47.62061], emitted as [38.8, 47.6]."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Release-date verification limitation: official CMS pages fetched this run provide historical publication dates and monthly reporting, but no calendar or announcement verifying December 15, 2026 for the August 2026 release. The registered resolutionDate remains 2026-12-15; it is unverified as an official publication appointment. Actual resolution follows the first publication of the specified O row."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The upside risk is a rebound in electronic verification success or a renewal cohort with more administratively renewable beneficiaries; a recovery above 47.6% would land outside the interval. The downside risk is continued deterioration in cohort matching or more renewals remaining pending at month-end; a fall below 38.8% would land outside the interval. A change in Georgia's treatment of renewals following changed circumstances could also move the published share beyond these bounds."
      },
